  "method": "Independent mathematical reading of HTW9\u2013HTW14 and HTW20\u2013HTW24, direct comparison with the literal original structures and producers, and independent git-pin/file/range/block hash verification. No Lean replay or theorem-name-only matching is claimed.",
  "mathematical_checks": [
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW9"
      ],
      "finding": "The spherical alternative of HTW6 applies without a nonresonance assumption. The normalized U_i=Q^i Theta(e_i(x)) roots and signed coefficient (-1)^k P_{n-k} agree with SymOfVieta/LevSymOf and the inherited BCS15/UPA normalization. Classical vector separation descends the equality on the actual maximal-compact fixed base module."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW10"
      ],
      "finding": "The finite subset-indexed a_T,b_T family expands exactly to product_{i<k}(X_k-X_{w(i)}). A nonidentity permutation has i<w(i), yielding the zero factor. Alternation and universal integral cancellation give both dual expansions; no factorial, Vandermonde, or residue characteristic is inverted."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW11"
      ],
      "finding": "The Bernstein relations and polynomial action have the exact original orientation in HkDefs/IwBernHk. E=sum_w T_w gives partial(N_Q f), with the longest-permutation coefficient fixing normalization. The integral sandwich identity and spherical-vector identity retain the unnormalized compact trace. The two identities pass to the actual Hecke algebra/module, and separate places commute."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW12"
      ],
      "finding": "The actual inclusion and product trace give the stated polynomial-semilinear maps. Symmetric coefficients descend through the ordered splitting relations. The two dual expansions establish balanced Casimir and hence reverse-map semilinearity over each variable; the two compositions are exactly product_j N_{Q_j}. No surjectivity of beta or flatness of M0 is assumed."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW13"
      ],
      "finding": "Each N_Q factor is literally among the ordered-pair factors of fEl. Multiplying only the reverse map by the remaining integral polynomial changes both compositions to the full original fEl, without cancellation/localization or a square-free replacement."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW14"
      ],
      "finding": "Every original OpMod field is retained from the actual LevMod and HTW1/2: same coefficient ring/pair/base, finite module, projective diamond action, generator equation, exact trace kernel/surjectivity and U intertwining. HTW8 and HTW13 furnish all OpRel fields with the same n! exponent."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW20"
      ],
      "finding": "The two coefficient maps on Lambda agree on O and every original weight variable, hence on power series. Locality of O-algebra maps in IsCO is verified by the original ResMapBijective.res_map argument. The prescribed theta kills Y and sends X to the ordered root difference; the source constantCoeff identity and full pair naturality are exactly preserved."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW21"
      ],
      "finding": "The chosen completed module and diamond quotient of HTW17 have the literal TWRing action. HTW18/19 give the actual two maps on the augmentation quotient, and HTW16 extends their semilinearity to every completed coefficient. All TWMaps fields, including full-law trace evaluation for every group element/vector, have the unchanged n! exponent and full fEl."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW22"
      ],
      "finding": "The original global-data morphism is surjective, so its stipulated injectivity gives an actual continuous inverse. Pullback preserves the residual datum, determinant laws, local ordinary/polarization/type-kernel intersections, and the exact base map. Trace relations transport by inverse images of every group element; no module or coefficient replacement occurs."
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        "HTW23",
        "HTW24"
      ],
      "finding": "The LevelAlt base is chosen before the entire auxiliary family; the residual root lift is chosen before N. Every original TWPl place/prolongation/Frobenius/tame/congruence field is used on its actual level, followed by opTransport and opToTW. This gives all literal TWAut/HasAut quantifiers on the same ideal. Empty auxiliary families, the abstract rank-zero case, and the actual positive-rank HLM26 application do not introduce a prime exclusion."
    }
  ],
  "scope_limits": [
